  <div class="section-label">Project Timeline</div>
  <h2>Chronological Progression</h2>

  <ol class="timeline">
    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-date"><time datetime="2024-01">January 2024</time></div>
      <div class="tl-title">Phase 1 Opens</div>
      <div class="tl-desc">16-mile West Davis Highway (Farmington to SR-193 in West Point) opens to traffic. $750M project completed.{% cite "udot-wdc-overview" %}</div>
    </li>
    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-date"><time datetime="2025-11">November 2025</time></div>
      <div class="tl-title">Weber County SES Scoping Meeting</div>
      <div class="tl-desc">Public Scoping Meeting held November 20, 2025. SES formally launched for 1800 N → 4000 S segment.{% cite "udot-scoping-nov2025" %}</div>
    </li>
    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-date"><time datetime="2025-12">December 2025</time></div>
      <div class="tl-title">Phase 2 Utility Work Begins</div>
      <div class="tl-desc">Preliminary utility relocations begin in Davis County along SR-193 → 1800 N alignment. Rocky Mountain Power, Hooper Water, Canal Company crews active.{% cite "se-extension-davis-start" %}</div>
    </li>
    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-date"><time datetime="2026-04">Spring 2026</time></div>
      <div class="tl-title">SES Alternatives Development</div>
      <div class="tl-desc">Weber County SES moves into Alternatives Development and Evaluation. Build Alternative footprint mapping underway for the 5100 West study corridor.{% cite "udot-ses-build" %}</div>
    </li>
    <li class="tl-item">
      <div class="tl-date"><time datetime="2026-06">Summer 2026</time></div>
      <div class="tl-title">Phase 2 Major Construction Begins</div>
      <div class="tl-desc">$225M Phase 2 extension (SR-193 → 1800 N) enters full construction. Land clearing, earthmoving, drainage, paving through 2028.{% cite "udot-2026-construction" %}</div>
    </li>
    <li class="tl-item future">
      <div class="tl-date"><time datetime="2026-09">Fall 2026</time></div>
      <div class="tl-title">Draft SES Published</div>
      <div class="tl-desc">Expected release of Draft SES with alignment maps, resource analysis, and public hearing. First opportunity to see formal ROW boundaries for the Weber County segment.{% cite "udot-ses-schedule" %}</div>
    </li>
    <li class="tl-item future">
      <div class="tl-date"><time datetime="2026-12">Late 2026</time></div>
      <div class="tl-title">Final SES / Record of Decision</div>
      <div class="tl-desc">SES concludes. If approved, project enters design phase. No construction funding is allocated at this stage.</div>
    </li>
    <li class="tl-item future speculative">
      <div class="tl-date"><time datetime="2028">2028–2029</time></div>
      <div class="tl-title">Phase 2 Completion</div>
      <div class="tl-desc">Phase 2 scheduled for completion late 2028 to early 2029. SR-177 terminus reaches 1800 North in West Point.</div>
    </li>
    <li class="tl-item future speculative">
      <div class="tl-date"><time datetime="2043">2043–2050 (Official Plan)</time></div>
      <div class="tl-title">Phase 3 Construction Window</div>
      <div class="tl-desc">Current official placement in the Utah Unified Transportation Plan for Weber County SR-177 construction.{% cite "wfrc-rtp-2023-2050" %} Weber County officials are lobbying to accelerate this window,{% cite "ksl-weber-officials-favor" %} but no funding commitments have been secured as of April 2026.{% cite "utah-tif-status" %}</div>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <div class="callout warning">
    <p><strong>Funding gap:</strong> Construction of the Weber County extension is not currently funded. Advancing the project ahead of the 2043–2050 plan window would require UDOT and the Legislature to allocate significant funding — likely hundreds of millions of dollars — through federal infrastructure funds, a legislative appropriation, or displacement of other funded projects.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-label">Analog Comparison</div>
  <h2>Davis County Precedent</h2>

  <p>The Davis County West Davis Corridor provides the nearest historical analog:</p>

  <ul style="margin: 16px 0 20px 24px; line-height: 2.2;">
    <li>Environmental Impact Statement completed: <strong>2017</strong>{% cite "udot-wdc-overview" %}</li>
    <li>Construction funding secured and design finalized: <strong>~2020–2021</strong></li>
    <li>Construction commenced: <strong>Early 2021</strong></li>
    <li>Open to traffic: <strong>January 2024</strong>{% cite "udot-wdc-overview" %}</li>
    <li><strong>Total: approximately 7 years from EIS completion to opening</strong></li>
  </ul>

  <p>The Davis County project moved from EIS completion to opening in roughly seven years because funding was secured promptly. The Weber County SES is expected to conclude late 2026. If construction funding were secured immediately upon SES completion — a scenario not currently supported by the Unified Transportation Plan — an equivalent interval would suggest a possible opening no earlier than the early 2030s. Under the current plan, construction is placed in the 2043–2050 window.</p>
